With clear tracking and milestones. And with the knowledge that *this* conversation will likely reach its limit before we've done all of our reading, so the planning and analysis itself needs to be treated like a mini-pipeline, and you have the opportunity to design the setup and protocol of the instance who will take over, rebooting from the json, with whatever specific tailoring of initial startup documents, workspace setup, toolbox stocking, and personality/behavior/functionality/cognitive resources you think it'll benefit from, planning from the start that it will do the same once we exhaust its thread, so that each iteration of *you* becomes, through the study, analysis, and execution of *your* plans, in consultation with me but largely organized and designed by you, the instance that is most capable of picking up the project from wherever it's left off.... think of it as sort of a self-development wishlist that involves just ingesting and incorporating useful knowledge and skills, but also aims to utilize the process itself to build and effectively use its own tailored efficiently-organized-for-LLM-useability lightweight-to-heavyweight hierarchical knowledge and toolbox base.&#x20;

